libsomrando
===========

C port of the vanilla-mode generator of Moppu/SecretOfManaRandomizer v1.49 (commit 1404b7b),
https://github.com/Moppu/SecretOfManaRandomizer, Copyright (c) Moppleton and contributors.
Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version.
The full text is in COPYING.LIB.  Every source file in src/ is derived from, or written to reproduce
byte-for-byte, the upstream C# files named in its header comment; those notices are kept.

Third-party material carried over from upstream
  * DotNet110Random (src/sr_random.c): a re-implementation of the .NET Framework System.Random algorithm
    (Knuth subtractive generator); the upstream C# class carries an MIT notice from Microsoft, kept in that file.
  * HashcodeUtil.GetDeterministicHashCode (src/sr_random.c): upstream helper of unknown origin, ported as is.

Provenance of every embedded or build-time table (checked 2026-10-20 with tests/scan_rom_bytes.py: no 32-byte window of the vanilla ROM in any binary)

  Derived from the Secret of Mana ROM (Square, 1993).  Never stored and never linked whole:
    * Vineshroom tile data (3584 bytes, upstream Resources/vineshroom_tiles.bin), the Ancient Cave map palette sets (13 x 210 bytes,
      Resources/mapPalettes/ac*), the boss rush rest-map palette set (210 bytes) and the two Ancient Cave custom maps (1024 and 624 bytes,
      Resources/customMaps/acManafort*): upstream made them by editing dumps of the game, so parts are byte-identical to the ROM.
      src/sr_rom_recipes.c (generated by tools/gen_rom_recipes.py) keeps, for each, ROM offsets and lengths plus the bytes that differ from the
      ROM (the upstream author's edits, LGPL-2.1+) and a CRC-32.  sr_rom_res() (src/sr_rom_res.c) rebuilds the resource from the user's own ROM at
      run time and refuses a ROM whose bytes give another CRC.  The literals hold no run of 12 or more ROM bytes with at least 4 different values.
  Original third-party data, not ROM data (verified: no 16-byte window in common with the ROM except by chance):
    * Ancient Cave quote text, data/sr_quotes_*.c: see data/README.quotes.md.
    * Boss rush rest map layers (2 x 3500 bytes, sr_p2_bossrush_data.c), difficulty presets, boss tables, Manafort room patterns and the event
      difference tables: constants of the upstream sources (LGPL-2.1+, Moppleton), no ROM bytes.
  Third-party data generated at build time from an upstream checkout (SOM_RANDO_SRC), not stored in this repository, not ROM data:
    * Pokedex names and descriptions (Resources/pokedata3.xml, tools/gen_p4_ev1_resources.py): text about Nintendo / Game Freak characters,
      redistributed by the upstream project under its LGPL-2.1 repository; rights in the underlying text stay with their owners.
    * Nesoberi images (68 bmp files of Resources/nesoberi, tools/gen_p4_hmisc_resources.py): fan art by third parties, redistributed by upstream.
  Builds that omit SOM_RANDO_SRC cannot link the two generated files above; there is no ROM-derived fallback.

No ROM, and no data derived from a ROM, is stored in this repository or linked into a binary built from it.  The library reads the user's ROM at run time.
